# /deep-sleep — Agent Keep-Alive Mode

**Invoke `deep-sleep.sh` per the durable-request protocol.**

When the user says "/deep-sleep", "deep-sleep", "brb", or indicates they'll be away:

1. Read the Deep Sleep section in `~/.cursor/skills/durable-request/SKILL.md`
2. Call `deep-sleep.sh` via the Shell tool:
   ```bash
   bash ~/.cursor/skills/durable-request/deep-sleep.sh [timeout_minutes]
   ```
3. Default timeout: 1440 minutes (24 hours)
4. After waking, present a new checkpoint to the user

The user can wake the agent by running:
```bash
touch ~/.cursor/skills/durable-request/.deep-sleep-wake
```
